This is a Vite + React app serving smarthome dashboards. The smart home is Homey-based. It uses the `homey-api` npm package and an auth token for authorization to Homey. The app has pages for dashboards: 1st floor living room (`/`), 1st floor entre (`/entre`), and 2nd floor hallway (`/andre`). Dashboards run as Chromium kiosks on Raspberry Pis. The living-room Pi also runs this app (Express serves the Vite `build/` output plus `/api` routes).

Kiosk screens (landscape unless noted):

| Page | Pi | Screen |
| ---- | -- | ------ |
| `/` Stue | `pi@192.168.68.91` (also the app server) | Official Raspberry Pi 7" touch **v1**, **800×480** landscape |
| `/entre` | `rpi@192.168.68.99` | 13.1" touch, **1920×1080** (`min-width: 1900px` CSS) |
| `/andre` | Raspberry Pi **5** (not in `npm run deploy` yet) | Official Raspberry Pi **7" Touch Display 2**, **720×1280** portrait. Design `/andre` for this panel: touch-first, no hover. |

Requires Node.js LTS via nvm (`.nvmrc` = `lts/*`, `package.json` engines `^24.19.0`). The smart home also posts data to an MQTT server.

## Tooling

- Build/dev: Vite + API (`npm start` / `npm run dev`; Vite on 3000, API on 3080, `/api` proxied)
- Production server: `npm run start:production` (Express on `PORT`, default 80)
- API only: `npm run start:api` (port 3080)
- Lint/format/test: `npm run lint`, `npm run format`, `npm run test`
- Health check: `npm run verify` (expects HTTP 200 on `/`, `/entre`, `/andre`, `/api/read/temperature/loft`, `/api/read/weather`, `/api/read/departures`)
- Production deploy: `npm run deploy` from your Mac (`scripts/deploy.sh`) — two Raspberry Pi kiosks, SSH keys only (see `.cursor/rules/deploy.mdc`)
